{title: 206 - Face to Face}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #206 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 206}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Edim]Face to face [Bb/F]with Christ my [Dm/F]Saviour, [F7]Face [Bb]to face, what will it be,
[Bb]When with rapture [Cm]I [F7]behold Him, Jesus Christ, who died for [Bb]me?
[Bb]Face to face shall I behold Him, Far beyond the [Cm/Eb]starry [Eb]sky;
[Eb]Face to face [Bb/F]in all His [Dm/F]glory [F7]I [Bb]shall [F7]see Him by and by!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[F7]Face to face shall [Bb]I behold Him,
[F/C]Far beyond the [Cm]starry sky;
[Cm]Face to face [F]in [Bb]all His glory
[Bb]I shall see Him [Cm/Eb]by and [Eb]by!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Edim]Only [Bb/F]faintly [F7]now [Bb]I see Him,
[Bb]With the [Cm]darkening [F7]veil between,
[Bb]But a blessed day is coming,
[Eb]When His [Bb/F]glory shall [F7]be seen.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Edim]What rejoicing [F7]in [Bb]His presence,
[Bb]When are [F7]banished grief and pain;
[Bb]When the crooked ways are straightened,
[Eb]And the [Bb/F]dark [Dm/F]things [Bb]shall [F7]be plain!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Edim]Face to [Bb/F]face! [Dm/F]oh, [F7]blissful [Bb]moment!
[Bb]Face to [F7]face to see and know;
[Bb]Face to face with my Redeemer,
[Eb]Jesus [Bb/F]Christ, [Dm/F]who [F7]loves me so.
{end_of_verse}
